    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473-a1">

                <pb facs="0823" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg729"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 107.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. F. Alexandre &amp;
                            Sons to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 23,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Since ours of the 28th ultimo in answer to
                    your esteemed and gratifying communication of the 27th ultimo, we have only
                    yours of 28th same.</p>
                <p>Now we beg to hand you the inclosed extract from our Vera Cruz agent (Mr. Juan
                    Ritter) of 8th instant, which confirms our several statements as to the positive
                    discrimination of the 2 per cent. less duties on goods ex Spanish line of
                    steamers, as allowed by the Mexican customs. The inclosed blank form from the
                    Vera Cruz customs-house clearly shows it, as explained in extract from our
                    agent, and which we think will have been confirmed by the American consul there
                    and by minister of United States at Mexico. Can you favor us with anything new
                    on this important question?</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Alexandre &amp;
                    Sons.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
